# ============================================================
# Smart Commerce & Supply Platform — Docker build exclusions
# ============================================================
# Context is the repository root (monorepo), so this file is the single
# gate that keeps credentials, local state and generated bulk out of every
# image. Introduced by P13 Phase 4.1; before it existed the repository had no
# container builds at all.
#
# What MUST NOT be copied in, and why:
#   .env*          real local credentials (JWT secrets, DB password, S3 keys)
#   node_modules   Windows-built native modules; the image installs its own
#                  from pnpm-lock.yaml on Linux
#   .next / dist   host build artifacts; the image rebuilds them
#   *.dump         database dumps
#   b2-test tree    a second copy of the repository (separate CI worktree)

# ── Dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
**/out/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
coverage/
**/coverage/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/
**/.cache/

# ── Secrets and local configuration ──────────────────────────
# Every .env variant is excluded, INCLUDING `.env.example`. Nothing in this
# repository loads a .env file at runtime (there is no dotenv/@nestjs/config), so an
# example file inside an image would be inert at best and mistaken for real
# configuration at worst. The documented templates live in infra/deploy/ and are read
# from the repository, not from a container.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# CI verification exception: deployment-invariants test checks this file exists on disk.
!infra/deploy/.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.kdbx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.secrets/
kubectl-config*

# ── Data dumps and local database state ──────────────────────
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.bak
pgdata/
postgres_data/

# ── Logs, scratch and evidence files ─────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
**/*.log
b1-*.txt
b2-*.json
p4-*.json
p4-*.log
p4-*.txt
p41-*.json
p41-*.log
p41-*.mjs
.p4-*
**/.p4-*
test-token.txt

# ── Binary office/spreadsheet test fixtures ──────────────────
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip
*.tgz

# ── Duplicate worktree and version control internals ─────────
apps/scs-platform-b2-test/
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Mobile toolchain (not part of a web/API image) ───────────
# Only the Flutter *build output* is dropped, never the `mobile/packages/` tree:
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` lists `mobile/packages/*` as importers, so excluding the whole
# `mobile/` directory would make `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fail on an importer
# mismatch. `mobile/build` and `mobile/.dart_tool` alone account for ~3 GB of the host
# working tree (APKs, native libs, dill caches), which is why they are excluded
# explicitly rather than left to the general `build/` pattern (which is root-anchored).
mobile/build/
mobile/.dart_tool/
mobile/.pub-cache/
mobile/.pub/

# ── Docs are excluded from images but keep the production
#    runbooks available to operators through the repository.
docs/

# ── Tests are not needed in a production image. Kept in the
#    build stage (the build graph may reference them), removed
#    from the runtime stage by copying only dist output.
